{%- liquid
  # The preview lives in Shopify Files so a release can swap the artwork
  # without a theme upload, and the picker still wins when a reviewer sets one.
  #
  # images['<missing>'] returns a TRUTHY drop rather than nil, so the old
  # `if strip` guard passed even when the Files entry was absent and sent
  # an unresolvable drop into image_url — Liquid renders that thrown error as
  # literal text inside the src attribute. Guarding on .width is the honest
  # test: a drop that did not resolve has no dimensions, so the whole figure
  # is skipped instead of shipping an error string as an image source.
  assign strip = section.settings.image | default: images['caddieinsight-report-preview-136534a.png']
  assign strip_alt = 'homepage.report.image_alt' | t
-%}

<section id="{{ section.settings.anchor | default: 'report' }}" class="sl-report" aria-labelledby="ReportTitle-{{ section.id }}">
  <div class="sl-report__inner sl-wrap">
  <div class="sl-report__copy sl-reveal">
    <p class="sl-eyebrow">{{ 'homepage.report.eyebrow' | t }}</p>
    <h2 id="ReportTitle-{{ section.id }}" class="sl-h2">{{ section.settings.heading | default: 'Numbers you can act on' }}</h2>
    {%- if section.settings.body != blank -%}
      <p class="sl-report__body">{{ section.settings.body }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      An ordered index, not a bullet list. These are the things you find in the
      report in the order you meet them, so the numbering carries meaning — and
      it keeps this section off the shared .sl-check-list, whose marker is an
      amber dot. Amber marks a value the engine measured; a list bullet is
      decoration, and decoration never gets the signal colour.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
      <ol class="sl-report__list">
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {%- assign marker = forloop.index | prepend: '0' -%}
          <li {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
            <span class="sl-report__list-num" aria-hidden="true">{{ marker }}</span>
            <span class="sl-report__list-text">{{ block.settings.text }}</span>
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ol>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  <div class="sl-report__media-wrap sl-reveal sl-reveal--d1">
    <div class="sl-report__card" aria-describedby="ReportDisclosure-{{ section.id }}">
      <div class="sl-report__head">
        <span class="sl-report__file">{{ 'homepage.report.file_label' | t }}</span>
        <span class="sl-report__sample">{{ 'homepage.report.sample_label' | t }}</span>
      </div>

      {%- if strip.width -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          The preview is mounted in a sunk well on the same 16px graph the
          hero's trace box uses, so the specimen reads as something laid on the
          instrument rather than a picture pasted into a brochure.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="sl-report__well">
          <img
            class="sl-report__strip"
            src="{{ strip | image_url: width: 1200 }}"
            srcset="{{ strip | image_url: width: 800 }} 800w, {{ strip | image_url: width: 1200 }} 1200w, {{ strip | image_url: width: 1600 }} 1600w"
            sizes="(min-width: 1000px) 640px, (min-width: 560px) calc(100vw - 200px), calc(100vw - 140px)"
            width="{{ strip.width }}"
            height="{{ strip.height }}"
            alt="{{ strip_alt | escape }}"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async">
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}

      <div class="sl-report__foot">
        <p class="sl-report__note">{{ 'homepage.report.priority_note' | t }}</p>
        <span class="sl-chip">{{ 'homepage.report.plan_chip' | t }}</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    {%- if section.settings.caption != blank -%}
      <p class="sl-report__caption sl-mono-label">{{ section.settings.caption }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    The three fields the sample report returned, pulled out of the card and run
    the full width of the section as a spec strip. It is the same 1px-gap
    bordered grid the hero readout uses, and the values carry the same amber for
    the same reason: they are what the engine handed back for this clip. The
    labels beside them are not measurements, so they stay mono and muted.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <dl class="sl-report__proof">
    <div>
      <dt>{{ 'homepage.report.club_label' | t }}</dt>
      <dd>{{ 'homepage.report.club_value' | t }}</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>{{ 'homepage.report.coach_label' | t }}</dt>
      <dd>{{ 'homepage.report.coach_value' | t }}</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>{{ 'homepage.report.practice_label' | t }}</dt>
      <dd>{{ 'homepage.report.practice_value' | t }}</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>

  <div class="sl-report__close">
    <p id="ReportDisclosure-{{ section.id }}" class="sl-report__disclosure">{{ 'homepage.report.disclosure' | t }}</p>
    {%- if section.settings.sample_url != blank and section.settings.cta_label != blank -%}
      <a class="sl-btn sl-btn--outline sl-report__cta" href="{{ section.settings.sample_url }}">{{ section.settings.cta_label }}</a>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
  </div>
</section>

{% stylesheet %}
/* No background of its own. Every neighbour that paints a panel hides the 8px
   technical grid body draws under the whole page; leaving this section
   transparent lets the grid run straight through the specimen, which is the
   one place on the homepage where that reads as the point rather than as
   texture. A single hairline is all the separation it needs. */
.sl-report {
  position: relative;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
  color: var(--sl-ink);
}
.sl-report__inner {
  padding-top: var(--sl-section-space);
  padding-bottom: var(--sl-section-space);
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: clamp(40px, 7vw, 64px);
}
/* Asymmetric and top-aligned, against the hero's centred pair: the copy is the
   narrow rail and the specimen takes the wide column, then the spec strip and
   the closing bar run the full measure underneath. */
@media (min-width: 1000px) {
  .sl-report__inner {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 4.6fr) minmax(0, 7.4fr);
    align-items: start;
    column-gap: clamp(48px, 5vw, 88px);
    row-gap: clamp(56px, 6vw, 88px);
  }
  .sl-report__proof,
  .sl-report__close { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
}

.sl-report__copy { min-width: 0; }
/* The eyebrow becomes a running head: label, then a leader rule out to the
   column edge. Base gives it the amber, which is wrong here — amber is
   reserved for measured values and a section label is not one. */
.sl-report .sl-eyebrow {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--sl-space-3);
  margin: 0 0 var(--sl-space-5);
  color: var(--sl-ink-muted);
}
.sl-report .sl-eyebrow::after {
  content: "";
  flex: 1 1 auto;
  height: 1px;
  background: var(--sl-border-strong);
}
/* The support rung, not the display rung. The hero owns the largest voice on
   the page; if every section below it shouts at the same size the page reads as
   ten identical bands again, which is the exact failure this rebuild is for. */
.sl-report .sl-h2 {
  max-width: 15ch;
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--sl-green);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-display);
  font-size: var(--sl-heading-support);
  font-weight: 800;
  letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  line-height: 1.02;
  text-align: left;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  text-wrap: balance;
}
.sl-report__body {
  max-width: 44ch;
  margin: 20px 0 0;
  color: var(--sl-ink-soft);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-lg);
  line-height: 1.55;
  text-align: left;
  text-wrap: pretty;
}

/* Spec-sheet index: mono ordinal in its own margin column, hairline between
   entries, no card and no shadow. */
.sl-report__list {
  margin: 28px 0 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
}
.sl-report__list li {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 40px minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: var(--sl-space-3);
  align-items: baseline;
  padding: var(--sl-space-4) 0;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
}
.sl-report__list-num {
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
  font-weight: 500;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  color: var(--sl-ink-muted);
}
.sl-report__list-text {
  color: var(--sl-ink-soft);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-base);
  line-height: 1.5;
  text-wrap: pretty;
}

.sl-report__media-wrap { min-width: 0; }

/* The specimen. Borders and a lit inset edge do the separating — a drop shadow
   is invisible on a near-black field, which is why the old 44px cast under this
   card was paying render cost for nothing. */
.sl-report__card {
  background: var(--sl-bg-card);
  border: 1px solid var(--sl-border-strong);
  border-radius: var(--sl-radius-lg);
  box-shadow: var(--sl-shadow-card);
  padding: var(--sl-card-inset);
}

.sl-report__head {
  display: flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: var(--sl-space-3);
  padding-bottom: var(--sl-space-3);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
}
.sl-report__file {
  flex: 1 1 auto;
  min-width: 0;
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: 0.16em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--sl-ink);
  overflow-wrap: anywhere;
}
/* No nowrap: a translated label longer than the head pushed the tag off the
   card edge rather than wrapping inside it. */
.sl-report__sample {
  flex: 0 1 auto;
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: 0.14em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--sl-ink-muted);
  background: var(--sl-night);
  border: 1px solid var(--sl-border-strong);
  border-radius: var(--sl-radius-sm);
  padding: 3px 10px;
  text-align: right;
}

.sl-report__well {
  margin-top: var(--sl-space-4);
  padding: var(--sl-space-3);
  border: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
  border-radius: var(--sl-radius-sm);
  background:
    linear-gradient(rgba(var(--sl-cream-rgb), 0.028) 1px, transparent 1px),
    linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(var(--sl-cream-rgb), 0.028) 1px, transparent 1px),
    var(--sl-night);
  background-size: 16px 16px;
}
.sl-report__strip {
  display: block;
  width: 100%;
  height: auto;
  border-radius: var(--sl-radius-sm);
}

.sl-report__foot {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: var(--sl-space-3) var(--sl-space-4);
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  margin-top: var(--sl-space-4);
  padding-top: var(--sl-space-4);
  border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
}
.sl-report__note {
  flex: 1 1 240px;
  margin: 0;
  max-width: 44ch;
  color: var(--sl-ink-soft);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
  line-height: 1.5;
  text-align: left;
  text-wrap: pretty;
}
/* The shared chip's border is an alpha of the logo green, which on this panel
   sits at roughly 1.1:1 and simply is not there. The chip is a claim, not a
   measurement, so it takes the structural rule rather than the signal. */
.sl-report__foot .sl-chip {
  flex: 0 0 auto;
  color: var(--sl-ink-soft);
  background: transparent;
  border-color: var(--sl-border-strong);
}

.sl-report__caption {
  display: block;
  margin: var(--sl-space-4) 0 0;
  color: var(--sl-ink-muted);
  text-align: left;
}

/* The spec strip. 1px gaps over a border-coloured bed, so the rules between
   cells are the grid itself rather than three separate boxes with three
   separate outlines. */
.sl-report__proof {
  margin: 0;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: 1px;
  background: var(--sl-border);
  border: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
}
.sl-report__proof > div {
  display: flex;
  align-items: baseline;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: var(--sl-space-4);
  min-width: 0;
  padding: var(--sl-dense-inset);
  background: var(--sl-bg-card);
}
.sl-report__proof dt {
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: 0.14em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--sl-ink-muted);
}
/* Amber, because these three are what the engine returned for the sample clip
   — the same rule the hero readout follows. */
.sl-report__proof dd {
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--sl-accent);
  font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
  font-weight: 500;
  font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  line-height: 1.35;
  text-align: right;
}
/* The three-up strip only where a cell is wide enough to hold "One plan with a
   pass mark" on two lines. Below that each cell is a key/value line, which
   reads better than three narrow columns of wrapped mono. */
@media (min-width: 1000px) {
  .sl-report__proof { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
  .sl-report__proof > div {
    display: block;
    min-height: 92px;
  }
  .sl-report__proof dd {
    margin-top: var(--sl-space-2);
    text-align: left;
  }
}

.sl-report__close {
  display: flex;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: var(--sl-space-4) var(--sl-space-6);
  padding-top: var(--sl-space-5);
  border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-border);
}
.sl-report__disclosure {
  flex: 1 1 34ch;
  max-width: 62ch;
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--sl-ink-soft);
  font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
  line-height: 1.55;
  text-align: left;
}
/* Bone on the field with a hairline edge. Amber here would claim the engine
   measured a button. */
.sl-report__cta {
  flex: 0 0 auto;
  width: fit-content;
  margin: 0;
}

@media (max-width: 749px) {
  .sl-report__copy { text-align: center; }
  .sl-report .sl-eyebrow { justify-content: center; }
  .sl-report .sl-eyebrow::after { display: none; }
  .sl-report .sl-h2 {
    max-width: 100%;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .sl-report__body {
    margin: 20px auto 0;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .sl-report__list {
    width: min(100%, 38ch);
    margin: 28px auto 0;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .sl-report__head { flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .sl-report__note {
    margin-inline: auto;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .sl-report__foot { justify-content: center; }
  .sl-report__caption,
  .sl-report__disclosure {
    margin-inline: auto;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .sl-report__close { justify-content: center; }
  .sl-report__cta {
    width: min(100%, 320px);
    min-height: 44px;
    margin: 20px auto 0;
    justify-content: center;
  }
}
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Report feature",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "anchor", "label": "Section anchor id", "default": "report" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "See the priority before you practice." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Body", "default": "Explore a sample report to see how CaddieInsight turns phone-video evidence into one priority, a focused drill, and a measurable pass mark." },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Key-position strip image", "info": "Shown inside the report card. Leave blank to use the versioned CaddieInsight report preview." },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "detail_image", "label": "Detail image (unused)", "info": "No longer shown — kept so older templates stay valid." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "caption", "label": "Mono caption under media", "default": "SAMPLE REPORT · DEMONSTRATION DATA" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "cta_label", "label": "Sample link label", "default": "View the sample report" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "sample_url", "label": "Sample report link" }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "point",
      "name": "Index entry",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "text", "label": "Text", "default": "Labeled key-position strip: address, top, impact, finish" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 6,
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Report feature",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "point", "settings": { "text": "See the selected club and capture context" } },
        { "type": "point", "settings": { "text": "Understand why one coaching priority comes first" } },
        { "type": "point", "settings": { "text": "Leave with a focused drill and measurable pass mark" } }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
